WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
A shopper checks out a ₹4,999 product. Customer expectation: one successful order.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Kubernetes starts replacing checkout Pod A. Existing traffic needs time to finish.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
The gateway uses a stale endpoint or connection. Shopper sees: “Could not confirm order.”

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
A later request reaches Pod B and commits the order. Shopper cannot know whether payment/order succeeded.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
The shopper retries the same logical purchase. Never treat a timeout as proof of rollback.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Drain Pod A; route new traffic only to ready Pod B. Result: reliable routing and one logical order.